course: dictionary
lesson: 12728
title: Drawn: pictures, pulling and ties
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Drawn is a form of the verb draw. You will often see it after have, has, was or were: «She has drawn a fox» or «The cart was drawn by a horse». Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: Drawn can mean made a picture with a pencil or pen, pulled along, or taken out. «The curtains were drawn» means they were pulled closed. «Two balls are drawn from the bag» means they were taken out of it.
explain: Drawn can also be an adjective. «Her face looked drawn after the long night» means she looked tired or worried. Notice that the sentence tells you how the face looked, not what it was made of.
fact: Drawn is a form of the verb draw.
fact: «Drawn» can mean made a picture: «He has drawn a rocket.»
fact: «Drawn» can mean pulled: «The cart was drawn by a horse.»
fact: «Drawn» can mean taken out, as in «Two cards are drawn from the pack» in probability.
fact: A game that is drawn ends with the same score for both sides, so it is a tie.
exercise: «The artist has drawn a tall tree.» What does drawn mean here? | Taken out of a bag | Ended with the same score | *Made a picture with a pencil or pen | Pulled along
exercise: «The cart was drawn by a horse.» What does drawn mean here? | Made a picture of | *Pulled along | Taken out | Tired and worried
exercise: Ella says «Her face looked drawn after the test.» What does drawn suggest? | *Tired or worried | Covered in paint | Happy and bright | A tie between two sides
test: «Two red balls are drawn from the bag.» What does drawn mean here? | Tired and worried | Pulled along by a horse | *Taken out | Made into a picture
test: «The football match was drawn, 2 goals each.» What does drawn mean here? | Taken out | *Ended with the same score for both sides | Made into a picture | Pulled along
exam: «The curtains were drawn, so the room was dark.» What does drawn mean here? | Tired and worried | Taken out | *Pulled closed | Made into a picture
